@mmoskal apologies, I know we had been circling around this for a long time. I'd actually forgotten about this proposal and probably should have revisited the discussions we'd had in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/5423, but V1 seemed like the right time to tackle it, since it fits well with the "persistent batch" approach.

You may have seen my recent RFC PR https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/13360 in that context which has a conceptually very similar interface. I was hoping to iterate on that design. I will take a look at this again as well as the prior discussions to see if there's things I've missed.

One thing that isn't worked out yet is how this would be used in conjunction with structured decoding, and whether the goal should be to encapsulate that entirely within a subsuming abstraction as you've done here or treat it as it's own thing. In particular w.r.t. the interaction with the scheduler and how fast-forward/jump tokens are handled.

